          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "Melikhov\n                                     All-Russia    Scientific   Research   Institute   for Fire  Safety\n                                            Russian   Ministry   for  Internal   Affairs\n                                                Moscow,   Russia\n\n\n                                   SUMMARY\n\n     The  flammability    in microgravity    of three  U.S.-furnished     materials,   Delrin,  polymethylmethacrylate     (PMMA),\nand  high-density    polyethylene,    was determined   using  a Russian-developed     combustion    tunnel  on Mir.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "Four  4.5-ram-\ndiameter   cylindrical   samples  of each  plastic  were  ignited  under  concurrent    airflow   (in  the direction   of flame  spread)\nwith  velocities   from  no flow  to 8.5 cm/s.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "The  test  results  identify   a limiting   air-flow   velocity   Vh,\"for each  material,\nbelow  which  combustion    ceases.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "Nominal   values   are V,,, <0.3  cm/s  for Delrin,   0.5 cm/s  for PMMA,  and  0.3  to\n0.5 cm/s  for  polyethylene:   These  values  are lower  than  those  obtained   in prior  ground   testing.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "Nevertheless,    they\ndemonstrate    that  flow  shutoff   is effective   for extinguishment     in the  microgravity   environment    of spacecraft.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "Micro-\ngravity   test  results  also show  that  the  plastic  materials   maintain   a stable  melt  ball  within  the  spreading   flame  zone.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "In general,   as the  concurrent   flow  velocity  V decreases,   the  flame-spread    rate  V, decreases,   from  an average   (for  all\nthree  materials)   ofV_: = 0.5-0.75  mm/s  at V = 8.5 cm/s  to V,: = 0.05-0.01  mm/s  at V = 0.3-0.5  cm/s.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "Also,  as V\ndecreases,   the flames  become   less  visible  but  expand,   increasing   the  probability   of igniting  an adjacent   surface.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "INTRODUCTION\n\n     The  results  obtained   in the  third  series  of nonmetallic-material      flammability    evaluations    in the combustion-\ntunnel  apparatus   Skorost  on  the  Orbital   Station  Mir  in space  are  presented   here.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "The  purpose   of the work   is to\nexpand  the  existing   database  on flammability    of melting  flammable   thermoplastic    polymers   in microgravity.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mate-\nrials  were  furnished   by NASA.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
