          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "The  interest   in this  issue   is explained  by  several\nreasons   (ref.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "8):\n\n               first,  combustion   study  in microgravity   makes   it possible   to compare   theoretical    results  against   test  data\n            directly,  which  leads  to progress   in combustion    theory;\n           second,  the  effect  of weak  processes   that  are overshadowed   on  the ground  can  be investigated    in\n           microgravity   due  to the almost  complete   lack of buoyant   flows,  which   is the most  important   feature  of\n          combustion    in microgravity,\n\n\n\n\n\nNASA/CR--    1999-209405                                  1",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "finallyandmostimportant,microgravity-combustionstudiescanleadtothecreationofadvancedfire-\n       safetysystemstbrspacecraftapplications,inparticularforsuchcomplicatedspacecraftastheInternational\n        SpaceStation(ref.9).",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "ThefireincidentsthathaveoccurredontheSpaceShuttleortheOrbitalStation(OS)Mir demonstrate    that  fire\n is a crucial  concern   in spaceflight    safety.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "The most  serious   operational   accident   in the history  of manned   orbital\n flights  was the  fire  incident   that  happened   on February   23,  1997  on the OS Mir.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "This  fire was  caused  by a Solid  Fuel\nOxygen   Generator   failure  as the result  of the  canister  burnout   during  generator   activation    in the Module   Kvant.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "A\ntragedy  was  avoided  only  due  to immediate   and  appropriate    reaction  of  the Russian  crew.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "It was also  helpful   that  the\nfire  occurred   in Kvant  when  the module  was  not overcrowded.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "The  situation  on Mir was  extremely   serious,  and\nimmediate    resolution   was  necessary.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "The crew  had  either  to  battle  the  fire,  or to abandon   the Space  Station  while\nexit  to the Soyuz  return  vehicle   through  Kvant  was  still  possible.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "The  flame  on the Oxygen  Generator   was  pointed   in\na certain   direction   with  a length  of ~0.5 m, and  the  temperature    of the combustion   products   in the flame  zone  was\nextremely   high  due  to the  constant   intake  of pure  oxygen.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "Sparks  and drops  of melting  metal  bright  white  in color\nburst  out  of the flame  zone.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "The  fire extinguished    within  a short  period  of time  (- 1.5 rain)  due  to the confident\nactions   of the Russian  crew, who  used  three  extinguishers    to eliminate   the  fire.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "For  the  International   Space  Station,   the  probability    of  fire  is greater  than  for the  spacecraft   of previous   genera-\ntions,  due  to the  higher  power  and  voltage   of the on-board   power  supplies  and  greater  volume  of scientific    instru-\nmentation   with  high-temperature     operation.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "Currently,    fire  safety  on Russian   spacecraft    is achieved  by prevention   methods   that exclude   the possibility   of\nfire through   a wide  range  of different   means,  for example:\n\n       •     selecting   structural   materials,   based  on the  results  of ground   testing,  with  priority  given  to\n           materials   with  higher  limiting-oxygen     concentrations     for combustion      (C,,,,,) or/and   higher  oxygen    indices;\n       •     specifying   nonflammable     materials   for the working  components    of the  electrical   systems;\n       •    maintaining   low oxygen   concentrations     in the  spacecraft   pressurized   compartment    during   the launch\n           phase:\n       •    decreasing   the  vent  flow  locally   in the area  of the  electrical   components    that might  be potential   sources\n           of  fire:\n      •     eliminating    potential   sources   of structural   material   ignition  by methods   of current   protection   or by use  of\n          nonflammable    instrumentation    and  cable  harnesses;   and\n      •     preventing   flame  spread   to materials   that  are tlammable    in an oxygen-enriched    environment.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "Lack  of buoyant   flow  in the  spacecraft   environment    reduces  oxygen   transfer   into the combustion   zone  and\ncombustion-products       transfer   in the  opposite   direction,   which  leads  to flame  extinction  on  the  surface  of solid  mate-\nrials when  the velocity   of concurrent   vent  flow  is low.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "Fifty  years  ago,  Zeldovich    (ref.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
