        {
          "text": "1.3 Evaluation   of Limiting  Flow  Velocity   for Combustion    in Apparatuses   with  Suppressed   Convection\n\n       It  is well known   that  the  natural  convection    in a thin  layer of gas  is suppressed    if the Rayleigh   (or Grashof)\nnumber  does  not exceed  a critical   value  (see  refs.14,   15, 23 and  24).",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 11,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
