          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "3.2 Concurrent   Flow  Effects   in the Flame  Zones  of Burning  Nonmetallic    Materials   in Microgravity\n\n     The  samples   tested  in the space  experiment    are  symmetrical.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 19,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "Therefore,   only  one  video  camera  Betacam  was\nused  to record  sample  combustion   through   the window  on  the  top of the combustion   chamber.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 19,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "The  other  camera\nrecorded   the control  board  to show  conditions   during  the  test (power   to the  fan  motor,  flow-rate   meter  knob  posi-\ntion, and  the number   of the sample   in the  midline).",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 19,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "Figures  3.1  to 3.12 show  the  results  of computer-aided     processing   of the video  information    obtained  from  orbit\nfor  all  12 samples.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 19,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "The combustion    parameters    that  characterize    a flame  and  a melting  zone  are a diameter   and\n\"length\"   of the molten  drop   (di,,/],),  a diameter   and  length  of the flame  (D,_, Lj),  a gap between   the flame  and  the\nsample   surface   (_:),  coordinates    of the  front  and rear  border  of the flame  (Xt:+,X,-),  and  the  heat  wave-front   coordi-\nnate  (1,_.), all shown  as functions   of time  v.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 19,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20000024924",
          "title": "Experimental Verification of Material Flammability in Space",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20000024924"
        },
        {
          "text": "All lengths  on  figures   3.1  to 3.12  are  dimensionless,    normalized   by\ndividing  by the sample   initial  diameter   (d,, = 4.5 mm).",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 19,
