          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Introduction\n            he flammability of solid combustible materials is typically characterized by their ignitability, flame spread rate,\n             heat release rate, and toxicity.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 1,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Although the most effective fire safety strategy is to prevent ignition altogether, if  T\n         ignition occurs the fire must spread to present a risk.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 1,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "For this reason, flame spread is one of the fire processes utilized\n\n           1 Postdoctoral Researcher, Department of Mechanical Engineering, University of California Berkeley, Berkeley, CA,\n        94720, USA.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 1,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
