          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "For the gas phase kinetic reactions, two different\n                                                       approaches   are   considered   independently   and\n                                                     compared.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 4,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Firstly, a  single  step,  mixing-controlled\n                                                       chemical reaction (mixture-fraction based combustion\n                                                     model) to simulate infinitely fast kinetics, meaning that\n                                                             the   reaction   rate   is  only  limited  by  species\n                                                             concentration.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 4,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Secondly, a  finite rate kinetic model\n                                                          defined by  a  single-step  second  order  Arrhenius\n                                                             reaction using the following kinetic parameters [26]:\n                                                          Asolid=1E10   1/s,      Esolid=125   kJ/mol,   heat   of\n                                                     combustion=16.7 MJ/kg, Agas=2.61E13 cm3/mol/s, and\n                                                        Egas=113 kJ/mol.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 4,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "In both cases, the products (CO2, H2O)\n                                                             are  lumped   into  a   single   species   to  reduce\n                                                        computational time.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 4,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "In  the work  presented  here  the hydrodynamic\n                                                    problem is calculated through the DNS mode, which\n                                                               calculates the heat (convection) & mass (diffusion)\n                                                                 transfer    directly,   not   through   semi-empirical\n   Figure 2: Schematic illustration of model domain.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 4,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
