          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Figure 3 (center) presents a frame with the light off and shows the flame\nburnout front as well some cotton residue smoldering after the passing of the flame.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 4,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Experimentally, the burnout front\nposition was defined as the upstream edge of the flame, which coincides with where the flame begins receding.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 4,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "During\neach test, after ignition is achieved, the flame spreads uniformly along the surface of the sample.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 4,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Usually, after the\nignition of the sample, as the flame spreads over the fabric it consumes most of the cotton, leaving behind some\nsmoldering cotton residue (bottom of Fig.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 4,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "3 (center)) that eventually burns out most of the fabric.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 4,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "As ambient pressure\nwas reduced, ignition of the sample was more difficult, and, in occasions, part of the cotton fabric would be left\nunburnt.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 4,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the FDS simulations, the pyrolysis front position is determined by tracking the solid surface temperature\ncorresponding to the solid material’s pyrolysis temperature which is selected as (𝑇𝑝= 350°𝐶 [36]).",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 4,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Flame burnout\nfront is determined in the FDS simulations similarly as in the experiments, by tracking the position of the flame when\n\n                                              4\n   International Conference on Environmental Systems",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 4,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "it starts receding from the surface.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Here the receding position is verified by Heat Release Rate (HRR) measurements\nand solid surface temperature measurements.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "The evolution of the pyrolysis front as a function of time is commonly\nused to determine flame spread rate.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "From the tracking of the position of the pyrolysis front, an average flame spread\nrate can be determined as a function of relevant ambient parameters (gravity level, pressure, forced flow velocity,\netc.).",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Because of the acceleratory characteristics of the upward flame spread, an averaged spread rate over the last\nportion of the sample (e.g.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "last 50% of the sample surface) is presented to minimize transient effects.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Figure 3: Schematics showing representative measurements for the experiments (left and middle side) and\nthe FDS simulations (right side).",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "B.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Effect of Reduced Ambient Pressure\n\n   Figure 4 shows a series of snapshots for both the simulation results and the experiments.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Figure 4 (top and middle)\nrow shows the heat released rate (HRR) per unit volume, which is proportional to the reaction rate, for cases with\ndifferent kinetic models in air at different ambient pressure.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Each image also includes the corresponding time stamp\nat which the snapshot was taken.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "As mentioned before, all simulations presented here are generated using the DNS\nmode.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "There are some clear differences in between the flames generated with infinitely fast chemistry and with finite\nrate chemistry.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the first case, when infinitely fast chemistry is assumed, it is expected that combustion will happen\nas soon as the flammable mixture is formed and, thus, the reaction is controlled only by the transport and mixing\nprocess of the fuel and oxidizer.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the second case, when a finite rate chemistry is considered, the model relies on the\nreaction rate following an Arrhenius reaction calculated from the kinetic parameters previously defined.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "From the\nresults shown in Fig.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "4 (top and middle) it is seen that chemistry is not expected to play a role at high pressures (~100\nkPa) since the flame propagation and burning process is mainly controlled by heat and mass transport, thus little\ndifferences between the two cases are observed.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "However, as pressure is reduced from 100 kPa to 30 kPa, the chemistry\nstarts to play an increasingly important role showing a lower HRR for both cases considered.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Furthermore, with the\nkinetic parameters considered, the finite rate chemistry model leads to blow-off after the flame gets away from the\nigniter at 50 kPa, and eventually no-propagation at 30 kPa.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "However, the experiments performed at 30 kPa still showed\nflame propagation, which indicates the kinetics are not well representing the case at very low pressures.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Figure 4 (bottom) shows snapshots of experiments performed at similar conditions of ambient pressure.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Flames\nspread visibly slower as pressure is reduced.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Interestingly, it is seen that experimentally as the ambient pressure is\nreduced the flame characteristics are also affected, becoming less turbulent and with its intensity reduced.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "As pressure\nis reduced, visible flame height is also affected, becoming shorter at lower pressures.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Further analysis of the model results shown in Fig.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "4 suggests that as pressure decreases, the HRR level (related\nto flame intensity) throughout the flame is also decreased.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "This is true for both fast and finite rate chemistry, although\nit is much clearer in the finite rate chemistry case (middle row).",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "On the other hand, the distance from the flame to the\nsolid surface does not seem visibly affected by the decrease in ambient pressure, regardless of the kinetic model, if far\naway from extinction conditions.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "These results seem to indicate that, in the FDS simulations, the reduction in flame\nspread rate with decreasing ambient pressure can be mainly attributed to a decrease in HRR.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "The decrease in HRR\n                                              5\n   International Conference on Environmental Systems",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 5,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "would reduce the heat flux that the flame transfers to the solid surface, establishing a reduced heat transfer feed-back\nloop until extinction conditions appear.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Figure 4: Comparison of FDS simulation results for heat release rate (HRR) of a spreading flame under\ndifferent ambient pressures and gas phase chemistry with experimental snapshots.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Top row corresponds to\nscenarios using infinitely fast chemical reactions, middle row shows cases using finite rate chemistry for the gas\nphase, and bottom row shows experimental snapshots.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "All cases correspond to an external 20 cm/s forced flow, normal\ngravity 9.81 m/s2 and 21% O2 concentration.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Figure 5 shows a comparison of the progress of the pyrolysis front and burnout front positions for three different\nambient pressures for both the FDS simulation results with infinitely fast chemistry and the experimental data.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "It is\nseen that, in spite of the simplifications included in the model, the simulations are able to qualitatively reproduce the\noverall behavior observed during the experiments: at lower ambient pressures the time evolution of the pyrolysis front\nand burnout front positions over the sample length  is slower, i.e.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "the flame spread rate is reduced.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "It is also seen that\nthe average total burn time for the experiments is larger than the one obtained for the simulations at all ambient\npressures tested.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the simulations, the reaction is initiated immediately as the igniter object is at a very high\ntemperature from the beginning, whereas experimentally, the flame spread process takes longer to start due to the\neffect of the heating up of the igniter and the sample at the different pressure conditions.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "These differences observed\nsuggest that the ignition process might not be entirely captured, causing larger differences at the beginning of the\nspread.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "6\n   International Conference on Environmental Systems",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 6,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Figure 5: Comparison of the time evolution of the (a) pyrolysis front position and (b) burnout front position of\nFDS simulations with infinitely fast chemistry and experimental data.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 7,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "The shaded area in the experimental\ndata represents the variability of the experiments.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 7,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "The pyrolysis front data from Figure 5 (a) is used to determine the flame spread rates.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 7,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Figure 6 shows average\nflame spread rate obtained as a function of ambient pressure for both the experiments and the FDS simulations.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 7,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Because of the size of the samples, and the accelerative characteristics of the flame, an averaged spread rate over the\nlast 50% of the sample is presented so that the data are closer to the steady state value and transient effects are\nminimized, as explained in section A.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 7,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Experimental and numerical flame spread rates decrease with ambient pressure,\nalthough only the results obtained with DNS and infinitely fast kinetics seem to agree well in terms of order of\nmagnitude.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 7,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "From the results, it is seen that the simulations performed using finite rate chemistry underpredict the\nexperimental spread rates at the higher pressures, while not even allowing flame spread at the lower pressure\nenvironments.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 7,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "This underprediction of the experimental data is likely associated with the selection of the chemical\nparameters chosen for the model and the differences that could exist between cellulose and the cotton fabric.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 7,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "It should\nbe noted that under this condition only partial burning of the sample near the igniter region was observed in the FDS\nsimulations done at 50 kPa, and the flame would eventually blow off about 11 mm away from the igniter, thus no\nspread rate was determined for that condition due to the very short propagation length.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 7,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Looking to decrease the effect of ambient pressure on the simplified global one step Arrhenius reaction rate, in\nRef.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 7,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "[37] different approaches were taken, looking into changes of the pre-exponential factor and the activation energy\nvalues as well as changes in the reaction order.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 7,
