          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "[37] the authors\nfound that a decrease in the activation energy (Egas) of about 4% increased the flame spread rate in about 0.8%, while\nan increase in the pre-exponential factor (Agas) of about 50% only increased the flame spread rate in less than 1.4%\naffecting in both cases very little the flame spread rate observed.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
