          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "as  the  flame  spreads.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 8,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Furthermore,  the\n  pyrolysis length can be correlated to the heat that is transferred from the flame to the solid.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 8,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Experimentally, this\n  pyrolysis length is obtained by subtracting the burnout front position from the pyrolysis front position.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 8,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the\n  simulation results, the pyrolysis length is determined similarly, by subtracting the burnout front position from the\n  pyrolysis front position.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 8,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Because of the accelerative characteristic of the spread process, the pyrolysis length is\n  obtained toward the end of the test when it is closest to steady state.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 8,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "Figure 8 shows simultaneously pyrolysis length\n measurements for both the experiments and the simulation results.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 8,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "The experiments and the FDS simulations show a\n  similar trend, with the pyrolysis length decreasing with decreasing ambient pressure and gravity level.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 8,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "It is also\n  interesting to see that the pyrolysis length seems to be more sensitive to changes in gravity than to ambient pressure.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 8,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "From these results it can be inferred that, despite the pyrolysis front spreading at similar rates between reduced gravity\n and reduced pressure conditions, the burnout front seems to spread significantly slower in reduced pressure\n environment that in reduced gravity conditions.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 8,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "In other words, the area affected by the flame preheating and\n  pyrolyzing the solid surface is more sensitive to reductions in gravity.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 8,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
