          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "As a comparison, the experimental data obtained in 1g at different ambient pressures and that of Saffire\nin microgravity are also included.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 9,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "It is seen that as the gravity level is reduced the flame spread rate follows a linear\ntrend, similar to what was observed when reducing ambient pressure (experimentally and through the simulations).",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 9,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "It\nis also seen that flame spread rates obtained at different gravity levels could be comparable to those obtained at\ndifferent ambient pressures.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 9,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20210017787",
          "title": "Determining the Cause of Reduced Concurrent Flame Spread over Thin Solid Fuels in Low Pressure and Low Gravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210017787"
        },
        {
          "text": "In such a case, flame spread rates under lunar gravity (0.17g) could be replicated by a\nreduction in ambient pressure to 46 kPa, and flame spread rate in a martian gravity (0.38g) would be similar to that\nencountered at 54 kPa.",
