          "nasa_id": "20220012861",
          "title": "Determining Flame Temperature By Broadband Two Color Pyrometry in A Flame Spreading Over A Thin Solid in Microgravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861"
        },
        {
          "text": "Espa˜na 1680, Valpara´ıso, Chile\n             cDepartment of Mechanical Engineering, University of California Berkeley, Berkeley, CA, USA\n                  dNASA Glenn Research Center, 21000 Brookpark Rd., Cleveland, OH, USA\n\n\n\n\n\nAbstract\n\nFire spread inside a spacecraft is a constant concern in space travel.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 1,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20220012861",
          "title": "Determining Flame Temperature By Broadband Two Color Pyrometry in A Flame Spreading Over A Thin Solid in Microgravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861"
        },
        {
          "text": "Understanding how the fire grows and\nspreads, and how it can potentially be extinguished is critical for planning future missions.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 1,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20220012861",
          "title": "Determining Flame Temperature By Broadband Two Color Pyrometry in A Flame Spreading Over A Thin Solid in Microgravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861"
        },
        {
          "text": "The conditions inside\na spacecraft can greatly vary from those encountered on earth, including microgravity, low velocity flows, reduced\nambient pressure and high oxygen, and thus affecting the combustion processes.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 1,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20220012861",
          "title": "Determining Flame Temperature By Broadband Two Color Pyrometry in A Flame Spreading Over A Thin Solid in Microgravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861"
        },
        {
          "text": "In microgravity, the contributions\nof thermal radiation from gaseous species and soot can play a critical role in the spread of a flame and the problem\nhas not been fully understood yet.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 1,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20220012861",
          "title": "Determining Flame Temperature By Broadband Two Color Pyrometry in A Flame Spreading Over A Thin Solid in Microgravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861"
        },
        {
          "text": "The overall objective of this work is to address this by studying the soot\ntemperature of microgravity flames spreading over a thin solid in microgravity.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 1,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20220012861",
          "title": "Determining Flame Temperature By Broadband Two Color Pyrometry in A Flame Spreading Over A Thin Solid in Microgravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861"
        },
        {
          "text": "The experiments presented here\nwere performed as part of the NASA project Saffire IV, conducted in orbit on board the Cygnus resupply vehicle\nbefore it re-entered the Earth’s atmosphere.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 1,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20220012861",
          "title": "Determining Flame Temperature By Broadband Two Color Pyrometry in A Flame Spreading Over A Thin Solid in Microgravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861"
        },
        {
          "text": "The fuel considered is a thin fabric made of cotton and fiberglass\n(Sibal) exposed to a forced flow of 20 cm/s in a concurrent flow configuration.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 1,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20220012861",
          "title": "Determining Flame Temperature By Broadband Two Color Pyrometry in A Flame Spreading Over A Thin Solid in Microgravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861"
        },
        {
          "text": "Reconstruction of the flame\ntemperature fields is extracted from two color broadband emission pyrometry (B2CP) as the flame propagates\nover the solid fuel.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 1,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20220012861",
          "title": "Determining Flame Temperature By Broadband Two Color Pyrometry in A Flame Spreading Over A Thin Solid in Microgravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861"
        },
        {
          "text": "A methodology, relevant assumptions and its applicability to other microgravity experiments\nare discussed here.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 1,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20220012861",
          "title": "Determining Flame Temperature By Broadband Two Color Pyrometry in A Flame Spreading Over A Thin Solid in Microgravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861"
        },
        {
          "text": "The data obtained shows that the technique provides an acceptable average temperature around\n∼1300 K, which remains relatively constant during the spread with an error value smaller than 117 K.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 1,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20220012861",
          "title": "Determining Flame Temperature By Broadband Two Color Pyrometry in A Flame Spreading Over A Thin Solid in Microgravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861"
        },
        {
          "text": "The data\npresented in this work provides a methodology that could be applied to other microgravity experiments to be\nperformed by NASA.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 1,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861",
          "matched_terms": [],
          "evidence_type": "extracted_source_text",
          "research_status": "unclassified",
          "classification_basis": "No recognized page heading found.",
          "classification_status": "requires_manual_review",
          "experimental_result_status": "not_established",
          "scientific_findings_verified": false,
          "nasa_id": "20220012861",
          "title": "Determining Flame Temperature By Broadband Two Color Pyrometry in A Flame Spreading Over A Thin Solid in Microgravity",
          "citation_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861"
        },
        {
          "text": "It is expected that the results will provide insight for what is to be expected in different\nconditions relevant for fire safety in future space facilities.",
          "source_field": "pdf_page_text",
          "pdf_page_number": 1,
          "source_url": "https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20220012861",
          "matched_terms": [],
